.TH DUPMAP 1 "September 2026" "dupmap 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dupmap \- terminal disk usage dashboard and duplicate report
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dupmap
.RI [ options ] [ path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dupmap
scans directory metadata at startup and displays the contents as a navigable
monochrome terminal dashboard. Fixed-size folder cards scroll vertically;
files and duplicate groups have separate views. Small files remain in their
real directories. Folder sizes are available after the initial scan, except
for unreadable trees. File contents are checked only when D is pressed.
The loading screen shows progress and elapsed time; Q quits during scanning.
The directory tree and duplicate results are cached for the session.
Wide-character ncurses supports Unicode names.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dupes [path]
Report duplicate files and estimated reclaimable space, then exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Show the program version.
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
.TP
.B Arrow keys
Select an item.
.TP
.B Page Up / Page Down
Move one visible page at a time.
.TP
.B Home / End
Select the first or last entry.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected directory or expand/collapse a duplicate group.
.TP
.B Backspace
Return to the parent directory.
.TP
.B 1 / 2 / 3
Open Dashboard, Folders, or Files.
.TP
.B d
Check duplicates on the first press, then open cached scan-wide groups with
scrollable member paths. Startup and ordinary browsing skip content checks.
.TP
.B Escape
Return from duplicates, close help, or cancel filter editing.
.TP
.B l
Open All items with direct folders and files together.
.TP
.B f
Edit the current view's filter. Enter applies, Escape cancels, Ctrl-U clears.
.TP
.B s
Cycle size, name, and modified-time sorting.
.TP
.B ?
Show keyboard help. Press ? or Escape to return.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH FILESYSTEM BEHAVIOR
Symbolic links are skipped and are never followed. Directories that cannot be
read are displayed as inaccessible instead of terminating the scan.
.SH STATE
When no path is supplied, the last directory and sort mode are loaded from
the dupmap state file under XDG_STATE_HOME, or ~/.config/dupmap/state.
